    {
      "item_id": "10722a9f-1262-53ae-8f73-11ff27be91d2",
      "session_id": "R3-23-what-happened-to-teleborian-in-the-end-of-the",
      "trace_id": "d8bdb8351ffeb8785ca0d24a49789948",
      "output": {
        "question": "What happened to Teleborian in the end of the court?",
        "answer": "During Salander’s trial, Edklinth testified that Teleborian’s psychiatric report was a sham, and the judge warned Teleborian that he risked a perjury charge. Police then arrested him in the courtroom for possessing about nine thousand child-pornography photographs on his computer and confiscated his laptop; he was led away as Salander watched. [E1] [E2] [E3] [E4]",
        "citations": [
          "[E1]",
          "[E2]",
          "[E3]",
          "[E4]"
        ],
        "reranked": [
          {
            "book": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest",
            "book_file": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest -- Stieg Larsson -- Millennium Trilogy #3, 2010 -- Random House, Inc_ -- a9a1c0e6f4b8fd47fa0771ff9463bc34 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "OEBPS/Lars_9780307593672_epub_c27_r1.htm",
            "paragraph": 440,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 27 Friday, July 15",
            "page": null,
            "text": "“Yes, I can. Dr. Teleborian’s report is a sham. It was put together with the help of a person by the name of Jonas Sandberg, just as he produced a similar document in 1991 with Gunnar Björck.”\n“That’s a lie,” Teleborian said in a weak voice.\n“Is it a lie?” Giannini said.\n“No, not at all,” Edklinth said. “I should perhaps mention that Jonas Sandberg is one of a dozen or so individuals who were arrested today by order of the prosecutor general. Sandberg is being held as an accomplice to the murder of Gunnar Björck. He is part of a criminal unit operating within the Security Police which has been protecting Alexander Zalachenko since the seventies. This same group of officers was responsible for the decision to lock up Lisbeth Salander in 1991. We have incontrovertible evidence, as well as a confession from the unit’s director.”",
            "paragraph_end": 443,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "ea3ebdda1eea37125c013dfa662ba33b326d24b40855af5da33075abe0c96ef4",
            "id": "ea3ebdda-1eea-3712-5c01-3dfa662ba33b",
            "agent_label": "E1"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest",
            "book_file": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest -- Stieg Larsson -- Millennium Trilogy #3, 2010 -- Random House, Inc_ -- a9a1c0e6f4b8fd47fa0771ff9463bc34 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "OEBPS/Lars_9780307593672_epub_c27_r1.htm",
            "paragraph": 444,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 27 Friday, July 15",
            "page": null,
            "text": "The courtroom was hushed, transfixed.\n“Would Dr. Teleborian like to comment on what has just been said?” Judge Iversen asked.\nTeleborian shook his head.\n“In that case it is my duty to tell you that you risk being charged with perjury and possibly other counts in addition,” Judge Iversen said.\n“If you’ll excuse me, your honour,” Blomkvist said.\n“Yes?”\n“Dr. Teleborian has bigger problems than this. Outside the courtroom are two police officers who would like to bring him in for questioning.”",
            "paragraph_end": 450,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "783ecba2c189f42add07607b74c69df9a589eb5f14cf14291eaf303921dcd1e6",
            "id": "783ecba2-c189-f42a-dd07-607b74c69df9",
            "agent_label": "E2"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest",
            "book_file": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest -- Stieg Larsson -- Millennium Trilogy #3, 2010 -- Random House, Inc_ -- a9a1c0e6f4b8fd47fa0771ff9463bc34 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "OEBPS/Lars_9780307593672_epub_c27_r1.htm",
            "paragraph": 454,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 27 Friday, July 15",
            "page": null,
            "text": "“And what is your business here?” Judge Iversen said.\n“We are here to arrest Peter Teleborian with your permission, and without wishing to disturb the court’s proceedings.”\nJudge Iversen looked at Advokat Giannini.\n“I’m not quite finished with him . . . but the court may have heard enough of Dr. Teleborian.”\n“You have my permission,” Judge Iversen said to the police officers.\nCollsjö walked across to Teleborian. “Peter Teleborian, you are under arrest for violation of the law on child pornography.”",
            "paragraph_end": 459,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "93ec354d2b66e5ece989e2c562096dad4e542fda6beeb7a41f448c5da28bc149",
            "id": "93ec354d-2b66-e5ec-e989-e2c562096dad",
            "agent_label": "E3"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest",
            "book_file": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest -- Stieg Larsson -- Millennium Trilogy #3, 2010 -- Random House, Inc_ -- a9a1c0e6f4b8fd47fa0771ff9463bc34 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "OEBPS/Lars_9780307593672_epub_c27_r1.htm",
            "paragraph": 460,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 27 Friday, July 15",
            "page": null,
            "text": "Teleborian sat still, hardly breathing. Giannini saw that all the light in his eyes seemed to have been extinguished.\n“Specifically, for possession of approximately nine thousand pornographic photographs of children found on your computer.”\nShe bent down to pick up his laptop, which he had brought with him.\n“This is confiscated as evidence,” she said.\nAs he was being led from the courtroom, Salander’s blazing eyes bored into Teleborian’s back.",
            "paragraph_end": 464,
